{'term_id': 'TERM-090', 'canonical_en': 'level difference', 'definition': 'The vertical height to be bridged between two floor or ground levels -- the rise a ramp, step or lift must overcome.', 'domain': 'circulation', 'scope_note': "Several sources condition a ramp's permitted gradient on it: Flemish decree Art. 19 bands by niveauverschil (REF-00995), the Australian step-ramp/long-ramp split at a 190 mm rise (REF-00997), REF-01004's ramp height as an independent variable, REF-01008's curb heights of 3, 6 and 9 in. Distinct from TERM-022 (level threshold), which is the zero-step doorway entry that removes a level difference.", 'created_at': '2026-09-25 04:58', 'created_by_session': 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa', 'updated_at': '2026-09-25 04:58', 'updated_by_session': 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa', 'catalogue': None, 'catalogue_entry_ref': None, 'catalogue_approval_ref': None}

{'term_id': 'TERM-091', 'canonical_en': 'ramp run length', 'definition': "The horizontal length of a single ramp flight between landings (the UK 'going of a flight').", 'domain': 'circulation', 'scope_note': "Sources condition the permitted gradient on it: Approved Document M Table 1 (REF-00992) by going, REF-01002 by its transit distance, REF-01005 Table 13's maximum horizontal projection of each run, Walter 1971's ramps as REF-01008 reports them. The mechanism is stated by REF-00996: effort is sustained longer on a longer run. Distinct from level difference, which is the vertical dimension. || AMENDED 2026-10-10 by session_2026-10-09-research-batch-24-parameter-pilot: scope_note was: 'Sources condition the permitted gradient on it: Approved Document M Table 1 (REF-00992) by going, REF-01002's 20 ft transit distance, REF-01005 Table 13's maximum horizontal projection of each run, Walter 1971's 10 ft and 20 ft ramps as REF-01008 reports them. The mechanism is stated by REF-00996: effort is sustained longer on a longer run. Distinct from level difference, which is the vertical dimension.'. The scope_note copied source-stated figures (a transit distance and two ramp lengths). A figure belongs in source_value_extractions with its locator, and a vocabulary row points at the sources rather than repeating what they say (rule 5); a figure in the vocabulary also biases what a scanner mines.", 'created_at': '2026-09-25 04:58', 'created_by_session': 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa', 'updated_at': '2026-10-10 00:24', 'updated_by_session': 'session_2026-10-09-research-batch-24-parameter-pilot', 'catalogue': None, 'catalogue_entry_ref': None, 'catalogue_approval_ref': None}

