{'adjudication_id': 2, 'observation_id': 18, 'outcome': 'NAMES-NEW', 'term_id': 'TERM-090', 'rationale': "NAMES-NEW. 'niveauverschillen' is the variable the Flemish decree conditions its gradient bands on ('tien procent bij niveauverschillen tot 10 cm'), and the same variable carries the permitted gradient in at least three other sources in this corpus under other names (rise, height, curb height). No term holds it, so a gradient stated 'for a rise of X' has nothing to point at for X. The English canonical is a literal gloss of niveauverschil, not a back-translated alias: the alias belongs to this Dutch observation, in its own language.", 'created_at': '2026-09-25 04:58', 'created_by_session': 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa', 'updated_at': '2026-09-25 04:58', 'updated_by_session': 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa'}

